WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.263
Hi, I'm Quoit!

00:00:02.263 --> 00:00:05.833
Vercel open-sourced an app that writes one web page per prompt.

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:08.429
The agent loop underneath is the interesting part.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.874
Every prompt and every step is stored first, so a new process

00:00:13.874 --> 00:00:16.362
continues a killed turn instead of starting over.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.920
Your message lands in the session log before the server accepts it.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.933
One worker holds the session.

00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:28.801
A replaced worker is refused at its next write.

00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:32.037
It calls the model, runs the tools, and writes each step

00:00:32.037 --> 00:00:33.062
back to the log.

00:00:33.482 --> 00:00:36.923
If the process dies, a new one replays the log and carries on.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.715
The hard case is a tool that was running when the process died.

00:00:42.135 --> 00:00:45.628
An idempotent tool runs again, under the same execution id.

00:00:46.048 --> 00:00:48.326
Any other tool never runs twice on its own.

00:00:48.746 --> 00:00:52.404
The model is told it may have partly run, and decides whether to check.

00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:57.926
Rerunning the turn pays for every model call again, and might refund twice.

00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:02.102
The log replays finished calls, and each tool says whether it may rerun.

00:01:04.342 --> 00:01:07.807
In fx0, the chat, Redis and Neon belong to the app.

00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:12.493
The libfx agent saves every step to Workflow World, and Vercel Queues

00:01:12.493 --> 00:01:13.915
restarts a crashed turn.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:18.978
On a fake local model, a kill inside a tool still

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.254
meant three model requests.

00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:22.808
A kill mid request re-sent only that one.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.939
On Vercel, a crashed function looks like a slow one, so recovery

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:30.253
can wait for the eight hundred second limit.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.882
One question for every tool.

00:01:33.882 --> 00:01:35.108
Can this run twice?

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:40.544
Store every step.

00:01:40.544 --> 00:01:41.521
Replay what finished.

00:01:41.521 --> 00:01:43.475
Rerun only what says it may.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:46.190
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:46.768
I'm Quoit.

00:01:46.768 --> 00:01:47.057
Bye!
